    37	
    38	**The design the strategy must map to.**
    39	
    40	1. *One document per pack, committed.* `starters/<record id with / replaced by __>__<pack>.json`
    41	   validates against `schema/starter.schema.json` (`starter/1`). Fields: `format`, `id`
    42	   (`<record id>/<pack>`), `record_id`, `title`, `summary`, `recipe` (id, repository, commit, tool
    43	   versions as name → version), `inputs[]` (name, sha256, bytes, origin: `verified` with the
    44	   verification run, or `deposited` with the custody key; E41 adds the deposited form, so slice 0
    45	   accepts both spellings and E41 fills the second), `decisions[]` (topic from a closed list: crs,
    46	   vertical-datum, depth-reference, depth-kind, units, nulls, domain, velocity, names; `value`;
    47	   `source` in publisher/data/chosen; `note`), `targets[]` (application from a closed list:
    48	   opendtect, resinsight, python; `version` the recipe ran against; `artefacts[]` with path, sha256,
    49	   bytes and the custody `href`; `import` naming the script or notebook artefact; `oracle` with
    50	   what was compared, how many values, how many differed), `licence` (computed: spdx, name,
    51	   attribution lines, share_alike), `fidelity` (path of the fidelity/1 document, committed beside
    52	   the pack), `built_at`. The documents are written by the recipe run (Ophiolite half of E42) and
    53	   committed here like outlines (OSD-D12); no job in this repository regenerates them.
    54	2. *Validity is several tests, each with its mutation.* (a) Schema validity. (b) Every input sha256
    55	   is a file of the record's latest verification inventory or a custody document of that record;
    56	   an unknown digest fails with the digest named. (c) The computed licence: spdx equals the inputs'
    57	   when they agree, share_alike true when any input is, redistribution of every input `allowed`;
    58	   a pack over a `restricted` or `unknown` input fails naming the input. (d) The decision log covers
    59	   every topic the pack's kinds need (wells need crs, vertical-datum, depth-reference, depth-kind,
    60	   units, nulls, names; a volume needs crs, domain, units, nulls; the mapping is a table in the
    61	   validator); a missing topic fails naming it. (e) Every target artefact has sha256 and bytes and
    62	   an `href` under the record's mirror prefix; a target without an `import` entry fails. (f) The
    63	   fidelity document exists, validates, and names every input sha256 with result converted or
    64	   partial; a failed input in fidelity fails the pack.
    65	3. *Build joins packs to records.* `build/catalog/starters.json` lists every pack with its targets,
    66	   licence and `href`s; each record in `records.json` gains `starters: [<pack id>]`. The
    67	   `collections.json` entry gains nothing in slice 0; STAC exposure is a named follow-on (out of
    68	   scope).
    69	4. *A manifest for a pack.* `osd manifest --starter <pack id>` writes a manifest/4 whose entries are
    70	   the pack's artefacts (href, sha256, bytes, licence, attribution), so `osd get` fetches a pack
    71	   like any selection and writes ATTRIBUTION.md. No new fetch code.
    72	5. *Fixtures first.* Two fixture packs under `tests/fixtures/starters/`: a complete F3-shaped pack
    73	   over fixture digests and a Teapot-shaped single-target pack; a frozen copy of starter/1 under
    74	   `tests/fixtures/schema/` the day it is written (hash pin, as for record/4 and verification/5).
    75	
    76	**Acceptance.**
    77	
    78	1. `make check` validates `starters/*.json` and the two fixture packs; removing one `decisions[]`
    79	   topic a well pack needs fails with that topic in the message (mutation per topic class).
    80	2. A fixture pack whose input digest is not in the fixture verification inventory fails naming the
    81	   digest; the same digest present in a custody fixture passes (two tests).
    82	3. A fixture pack over one input with `share_alike: true` and a computed `share_alike: false` fails;
    83	   over an input with `redistribution: unknown` fails naming the input.
    84	4. `osd build` on the fixture catalogue writes `starters.json` with both packs and `records.json`
    85	   entries with `starters` for exactly those two records; a third record has no `starters` key.
    86	5. `osd manifest --starter <fixture pack id>` writes a manifest/4 whose entries equal the pack's
    87	   artefacts by sha256, and `osd get` on it against a local transport fetches them and writes
    88	   ATTRIBUTION.md with the pack's attribution lines (reusing E06's local fetch test).
    89	6. `schema/starter.schema.json` has a frozen copy and a test that the frozen copy still validates the
    90	   fixtures.
    91	
    92	**Out of scope.** Writing a pack (Ophiolite half of E42); the deposited form's custody (E41); the
    93	site (E43); STAC Items for packs (follow-on when a STAC client is shown wanting them, evidence: an
    94	owner or user asking in an issue); counting downloads.
    95	
    96	**Stop rules.** The lane stops when a validity rule in design 2 cannot be tested without network or
    97	without Ophiolite code (the contract must stay offline and Ophiolite-free, ARCHITECTURE "no
    98	Ophiolite code runs here").
    99	
   100	**Ownership and dependencies.** Coding lane; paths `schema/starter.schema.json`,
   101	`tests/fixtures/schema/` (new frozen copy only), `src/osd/starters.py` (new), `src/osd/build.py`
   102	(starters join only), `src/osd/manifest.py` and `src/osd/cli.py` (`--starter` only),
   103	`starters/` (new directory, `README.md` only in this lane), `tests/test_starters.py` (new),
   104	`tests/fixtures/starters/**` (new), `docs/ARCHITECTURE.md` (one row for the Starters component).
   105	Depends on E07 (merged). Nothing else.
   106	
   107	**Evidence to inspect.** The validator's mutation list in the PR; `build/catalog/starters.json` on
   108	the fixture build; the frozen schema copy's hash.

